# Semantic callouts #semantic-callouts

NODX 1.0 includes a small set of semantic callout blocks. They are document
structures first; themes decide their final visual treatment.

:::summary {title="Available callouts"}
Use these blocks when the content has meaning beyond decoration: context,
advice, required information, risk, examples, or summaries.
:::

:::note
A neutral note for supporting information.
:::

:::info
Information a reader should notice while scanning.
:::

:::tip
Optional advice that helps the reader succeed.
:::

:::important
Essential information required to complete the task.
:::

:::caution
Potential negative consequences if the reader proceeds carelessly.
:::

:::warning
Serious risk or high-impact consequences.
:::

:::danger
Destructive, unsafe, or severe outcomes.
:::

:::example {title="Nested content stays normal"}
Callouts can contain regular blocks:

::code {lang="sh"}
nodx html document.nodx > document.html
::
:::

:::note {type="warning" title="Backward-compatible note syntax"}
The existing `note {type="warning"}` form remains valid and renders as the
same semantic warning callout.
:::
